<title>USA: Supreme Industries Inc Q4 net off, sales up.</title>
<headline>Supreme Industries Inc Q4 net off, sales up.</headline>
<dateline>GOSHEN, Ind. 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth Quarter			 Year</p>
<p>			1996	  1995	   1996	   1995</p>
<p> Revenues   $38,511,946 $35,208,602 $159,876,108 $164,450,979</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>Cost of sales</p>
<p>		 32,714,834  28,730,970  134,153,108  136,224,658</p>
<p>Selling, general and administrative</p>
<p>		  4,046,164   3,644,985   15,434,432   14,255,971</p>
<p>   Interest     382,412     343,780    1,530,624    1,781,350</p>
<p>		 37,143,410  32,719,735  151,118,164  152,261,979</p>
<p>Income before income taxes</p>
<p>		  1,368,536   2,488,867    8,757,944   12,189,000</p>
<p>Income taxes</p>
<p>		    588,000   1,005,000    3,671,000    4,949,000</p>
<p>    Net income  780,536   1,483,867    5,086,944    7,240,000</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>   Primary	    .08	   .17	    .55	    .84</p>
<p>   Fully diluted    .08	   .16	    .54	    .80</p>
<p>Weighted average shares:</p>
<p>   Primary    9,440,338   8,701,295    9,308,897    8,594,104</p>
<p>   Diluted    9,440,338   9,264,670    9,411,206    9,261,114</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q4 results hurt by start-up costs from a new fiberglass reinforced panel (FRP) facility in Ligonier, Ind., a new hardwood flooring facility in Honduras, and the three new distribution centers in Louisville, St. Louis, and Denver, as well as expenses related to the development of two new product lines. The total non-capitalized cost associated with these projects was $550,000 for the 1996 fourth quarter and $1.4 million for the full year, or $0.03 and $0.09 per share on a fully diluted basis.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
